{
  "slug": "privacypilot",
  "name": "Privacypilot",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Automatically generate Play Store-compliant privacy policies for Android apps. Scans your AndroidManifest.xml to detect every permission and your build.gradle to detect third-party SDKs (AdMob, Firebase, Crashlytics, etc.), then generates a complete HTML privacy policy covering GDPR, CCPA, COPPA, and Google Play Data Safety requirements. Deploys directly to GitHub Pages.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 skills**, **3 agents** and **4 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (5): `gdpr-compliance` (GDPR and international privacy law requirements for Android apps), `github-pages-deploy` (Deploying privacy policy HTML to GitHub Pages for Android apps), `permission-data-map` (Complete mapping of Android permissions to data types collected), `play-data-safety` (How to complete the Play Console Data Safety form accurately), `sdk-disclosure-rules` (Rules for disclosing third-party SDK data collection in privacy policies)\n- **Agents** (3): `manifest-reader` (Parses AndroidManifest.xml to extract permissions and app components), `policy-writer` (Generates a complete, Play Store-compliant HTML privacy policy), `sdk-detector` (Detects third-party SDKs in Gradle files and identifies their data collection practices)\n- **Commands** (4): `audit`, `generate`, `github-page`, `update`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install privacypilot@claude-community` from `SUDARSHANCHAUDHARI/PrivacyPilot`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 5,
    "agent": 3,
    "command": 4
  },
